 Netherlands to the north, Germany to the east, Luxembourg to the southeast, France to the south, and the North Sea to the west. Belgium covers an area of 30,689 km2 (11,849 sq mi) and has a population of more than 11.8 million; its population density of 383/km2 (990/sq mi) ranks 22nd in the world and sixth in Europe. The capital and largest metropolitan region is Brussels; other major cities are Antwerp, Ghent, Charleroi, Liège, Bruges, Namur, and Leuven.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belgium","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","iso2":"BE"}],"arc":{"reports":1,"first_seen":"2026-10-12T15:27:58Z","first_title":"Italy, German and Belgium push EU to cut red tape ahead of summit","first_url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMilwFBVV95cUxOREJnZ0RURzV5TERsNmFZY0tkNkJ5aFpyVFg4SmNSU3BPYmdxNzdRTkhSdE1aMHBGYlFxOEx3dUx1djJvUFljV0ZMcEE4Y3NrMFE2ZDM2MFNSNXhqbTZYa2Y3bzBmMlFzSUEtMElpbTU5OFlWa0tmXzliMmVWNmpHeUxnWUpxT2lQU3QzLWhrcndkcDhhQlRB?oc=5","first_publisher":"Decode39","earlier":[{"id":"e_52419f17919b","title":"Italy, German and Belgium push EU to cut red tape ahead of summit","date":"2026-10-12T15:27:58Z","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMilwFBVV95cUxOREJnZ0RURzV5TERsNmFZY0tkNkJ5aFpyVFg4SmNSU3BPYmdxNzdRTkhSdE1aMHBGYlFxOEx3dUx1djJvUFljV0ZMcEE4Y3NrMFE2ZDM2MFNSNXhqbTZYa2Y3bzBmMlFzSUEtMElpbTU5OFlWa0tmXzliMmVWNmpHeUxnWUpxT2lQU3QzLWhrcndkcDhhQlRB?oc=5","publisher":"Decode39","verification":"single_source_report"}],"weekly":[["2026-10-12",1]],"window_days":45}}}